    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32576" root="غو or غوى" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَوِىٌّ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَاوٍ</span>: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  and see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَوًى</span>. You
say of a hungry person, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَأَيْتُهُ غَوِيًّا مِنَ الجُوْعِ</span> [<i>I
saw him empty,</i> or <i>lean, from hunger</i>]; like as
one says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوِيًا</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَوِيًا</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَاوِيًا</span>] and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَوِيًا</span>.
(TA.)

